When the window that shows a tab preview is deactivated, Ladybird now
hides the preview, and an inactive window opens none. Chromium hides
its hover card the same way: TabStrip::OnWidgetActivationChanged() calls
UpdateHoverCard(nullptr, ...), which ends in TabHoverCardController::
HideHoverCard(). Firefox rolls its preview panel up as soon as the
window resigns key (nsCocoaWindow’s “windowDidResignKey:” calls
RollUpPopups()), and its TabHoverPanelSet::shouldActivate() opens no
preview unless the window is the active one. Chromium, unlike Firefox,
does open a hover card in an inactive window.

Neither raises the preview’s window again as its image updates:
Chromium’s TabHoverCardController::OnPreviewImageAvailable() only
sets the thumbnail, and Firefox takes a single snapshot when the
preview opens. Both were read from source (Chromium e6c8d7c15aeb2,
Firefox 41db707342fe), not run.
